  "body": "### Summary\r\n\r\n#### Context\r\n\r\nThis PR fixes an issue related to the routing when using React InstantSearch Hooks with React Router.\r\n\r\n[FX-1925](https://algolia.atlassian.net/browse/FX-1925)\r\n\r\n#### Error reproduction\r\n\r\nUsing the [default state mapping function](https://github.com/algolia/instantsearch.js/blob/master/packages/instantsearch.js/src/lib/stateMappings/simple.ts), an error is thrown only on back navigation from a refined state, when reaching the initial / unrefined state:\r\n\r\n```text\r\ndefaultStateMapping.ts:10 Uncaught TypeError: Cannot destructure property 'configure' of 'uiState' as it is null.\r\n    at getIndexStateWithoutConfigure (defaultStateMapping.ts:10:11)\r\n    at defaultStateMapping.ts:36:24\r\n    at Array.reduce (<anonymous>)\r\n    at Object.routeToState (defaultStateMapping.ts:32:38)\r\n    at createRouterMiddleware.js:45:57\r\n    at _onPopState (history.js:140:11)\r\n```\r\n\r\nCodeSandbox error reproduction: https://codesandbox.io/s/rish-with-react-router-simple-state-mapping-error-k6xqkn\r\n\r\nVideo reproduction of the error:\r\n\r\nhttps://user-images.githubusercontent.com/662153/206485747-ef4b2045-c5ac-470b-9799-45063a3d7216.mov\r\n\r\n#### Cause of the issue\r\n\r\nWhen you navigate to the `/search` route, React Router [push some history state data](https://github.com/remix-run/react-router/blob/b67538b1172c3dcf07a2e431bbe7c2eb32b06eaf/packages/router/history.ts#L591) along with the new URL:\r\n```js\r\n{ usr: null, key: '4ykrr3bq' }\r\n```\r\n\r\nIn the simple state mapping function, in the `routeToState` function, we reduce the history state assuming the key is the `indexId` and the value is the state. But using React Router, the first key is `usr`, so the corresponding value `null` is passed to the `getIndexStateWithoutConfigure` function.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/algolia/instantsearch.js/blob/8c68f37364f4199b9be76fa7ddd3fc1aea596d6a/packages/instantsearch.js/src/lib/stateMappings/simple.ts#L27-L35\r\n\r\nThis function then tries to deconstruct the `configure` object from the `uiState` but since it's `null`, it throws an error.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/algolia/instantsearch.js/blob/8c68f37364f4199b9be76fa7ddd3fc1aea596d6a/packages/instantsearch.js/src/lib/stateMappings/simple.ts#L3-L8\r\n\r\n### Result\r\n\r\nWe always read the state from the URL because the state of the history can be incorect in some cases (e.g. using React Router) so no more error is thrown.",
